The Rook package uses R's built-in "help server", which is known to have issues. The httpuv <http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/httpuv/index.html> package provides an alternative implementation of Rook and it is much more reliable.

Alternatively look at some high-level packages like opencpu <http://opencpu.org> or shiny, which take care of all this low-level stuff so you don't have to worry about it at all.

